    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change I implemented.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe identity key was redesigned so that `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`, and duplicate/soft-match detection now flows from that key.\n\n### 1. New identity key \u2014 `OwnerMapper.toIdentityKey`\nNow returns the lower-case 64-hex SHA-256 digest of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (previously the plain `telephone|email|householdId` string). This is the field exposed in `OwnerDto.identityKey` and the key the 409 check compares.\n\n### 2. New helper class \u2014 `mapper/OwnerIdentity.java`\nHolds `sha256Hex(String)` and a standard American `soundex(String)` implementation. I put these in a separate class rather than on the `OwnerMapper` interface because MapStruct otherwise treats `String\u2192String` methods as candidate property mappings (that was the first compile failure).\n\n### 3. Soft-match trigger \u2014 `markPossibleDuplicate` in the controller\nRewrote it to flag `possibleDuplicate` when an existing (non-deleted) owner has the **same `soundex(lastName)` and same `postcode`** but a **different `identityKey`** \u2014 picking the earliest matching id. Declared household members (`sharesHousehold`) and owners with no postcode are never flagged. Consequently two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones are no longer a hard 409 \u2014 they now surface as a soft match.\n\n### 4. Duplicate detection unchanged in shape\n`requireUniqueIdentity` still rejects with 409 only on an exact `identityKey` collision, still ignores soft-deleted owners, and the email-domain blocklist still runs first (in `normalizeEmail`). There was no separate household 409 block to remove \u2014 it had already been consolidated into the single identity key.\n\n### 5. Docs\nUpdated the `identityKey` description in `openapi.yml` and the javadocs on `requireUniqueIdentity`, `DuplicateIdentityException`, and `ExceptionControllerAdvice` to describe the new formula.\n\nBoth the existing/new acceptance tests (`coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` asserting the 64-hex shape, and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` asserting the collision \u2192 409) pass, and the full suite is green.",
